Subject: Reading Wireless Newt Jupiter Brains

Somebody mentioned:
"..... a couple of the apps we're considering involve paging/wireless 
network technology..."

This reminds me of a question that has been developing in my mind for 
some time, regarding the possible future effects upon our own 
biological systems, most importantly our ears & brains, from all the 
electronic waves being transmitted about in the atmosphere from 
wireless devices, including telephones, televisions, Newtons & such.

I don't know enough about how our brains work on the minute electrical 
level, but I have considered whether this increase of structured 
electrical impulses moving through the air could perhaps create a 
confusion in the mental state of those through whom it passes,  
disturbing the  conduction of one's own thought processes as they 
attempt to make their synaptic contact.

(Or else we could learn to "read" these signals, and then life would be 
hell, if one didn't know how to hang up.)

At least, it would be necessary to learn how to maintain one's 
intellectual composure, distinguishing one's own 'sense' of one's own 
intelligence while synthesizing, sifting through myriad ideas and 
fleeting thoughts, and not confuse any interruptions which come through 
as a personal inability to think straight.

Blanc






